WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.090
- Good morning, Hank. It's Tuesday.

00:00:01.090 --> 00:00:02.100
- Huhhhhhhhh.

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:04.200
- Oh, it's some kind of reunion video.

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:05.970
- Hi.
- Okay, this is a very special edition

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:08.040
of Question Tuesday in which I ask you questions

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:11.018
that contain the word first.

00:00:11.018 --> 00:00:12.690
- Just like the first comment does.

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:13.600
- That's actually my first question.

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:15.180
How do you feel about people writing "first"

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:16.600
in the comments of YouTube videos?

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:17.850
- It used to bother me, John.

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:18.760
- It doesn't bother me.

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:21.120
In fact, every time I am first--

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:22.300
- Yeah, right.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:23.390
- I can't stop myself.

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:25.210
- Right, it used to bother me until I was like,

00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:28.010
until I was first on a video
and I was like, (whispers) I have to--

00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:28.800
I want to do this.

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:30.100
- Hank, do you remember the first movie

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:31.000
that made you cry?

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:32.011
- American Tail.

00:00:32.170 --> 00:00:33.300
- I think it was American Tail.

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:35.680
Hank, what are your best first aid tips?

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:38.730
(both laugh)

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:40.130
- Call a doctor.

00:00:40.130 --> 00:00:41.010
- No! No!

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:42.689
Apply pressure to the wound!

00:00:42.689 --> 00:00:43.650
- What if there's no wound?

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:44.850
Just apply pressure.

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:47.500
- Yeah. (laughs)
- Pressure, pressure.

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:50.180
- That's-- I can confirm that's unpleasant.

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:52.115
Do not touch the couch under any circumstances.

00:00:52.115 --> 00:00:53.870
(Hank laughs)
This is an incredibly delicate setup

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:55.702
we've got, and it's not particularly straight.

00:00:55.702 --> 00:00:57.979
Hank, what was the first book you fell in love with?

00:00:57.979 --> 00:01:00.250
- Uh, (laughs) Jurassic Park.

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:01.380
- Really?
- Yeah.

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:02.793
(John grunts in disgust)

00:01:02.793 --> 00:01:05.280
Possibly the sequel.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:06.580
- The Lost World?
- Yeah.

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:07.680
- Wow.
(Hank laughs)

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:08.670
Really?

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:09.850
- I loved it so much.

00:01:09.850 --> 00:01:10.730
- Oh.

00:01:10.730 --> 00:01:12.440
For me, it was Gus is a Bug.

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:14.374
What was your first broken bone?

00:01:14.374 --> 00:01:16.300
- I think one of these.
- Incorrect!

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:17.470
- Oh you remember?
- I do.

00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:18.330
- What was it?

00:01:18.330 --> 00:01:20.059
- You fell out of a tree house,

00:01:20.059 --> 00:01:21.860
and you broke your arm.

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:22.760
- No, I did not.

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:24.244
- You did.
- I did not.

00:01:24.244 --> 00:01:25.398
-You definitely did.

00:01:25.398 --> 00:01:26.900
- Call Mom.
- Okay.

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:28.600
- Did I ever fall out of a tree, Mom?

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:29.950
Do you ever remember me breaking a bone--

00:01:29.950 --> 00:01:31.260
- A tree house!
- falling out of a tree?

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:32.250
- A tree house.

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:33.740
- [Mom] No.
(John groans)

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:35.240
- [Mom] John fell out of a tree house.

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:36.470
- Who did?

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:37.940
- [Mom] John.

00:01:37.940 --> 00:01:38.940
- Oh!

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:40.540
- You fell out of a tree house?

00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:41.820
- It's a memory of myself.

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:44.410
(Hank and Mom laugh)

00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:45.980
- Funny how brains work.

00:01:45.980 --> 00:01:48.135
- Hank, what was your first concert?

00:01:48.135 --> 00:01:51.220
- I think it was probably They Might Be Giants.

00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:53.340
- I think it was They Might Be Giants. I remember it.

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:54.650
You were young. You were like 11.

00:01:54.650 --> 00:01:56.137
- Okay, you were there?
- Yeah.

00:01:56.137 --> 00:01:58.090
- My first concert may have been the B-52s

00:01:58.090 --> 00:01:59.492
now that I'm thinking about it.

00:01:59.492 --> 00:02:01.770
- I think the B-52s opened for the Violent--

00:02:01.770 --> 00:02:04.410
- [Both] The Violent Femmes opened for the B-52s.

00:02:04.410 --> 00:02:06.510
- Hank, do you remember the first time you saw snow fall?

00:02:06.510 --> 00:02:08.120
- I remember the first time I saw snow

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:09.980
on the ground in Alabama.

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:12.610
And I was like there it is! It's a thing!

00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:14.010
- The first time I saw snow fall,

00:02:14.010 --> 00:02:15.980
I was fully like 9 or 10 years old,

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:18.510
and I was astonished,

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:21.570
because I thought snowflakes were like the ones

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:23.260
that you make in elementary school--
- Like cut out?

00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:25.040
Yeah.
- I thought they were about that big.

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:26.570
- I thought they were made up.

00:02:26.570 --> 00:02:28.480
(John laughs)
I thought they were a made-up idea,

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:29.462
and then I saw a snowflake,

00:02:29.462 --> 00:02:31.900
and I was like, it's the shape!

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:32.760
- Yeah.

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:34.040
I thought that about moonlight.

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:36.400
I thought that--
- I also thought that about--

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:39.100
this is weird, because we live in like street light central,

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:41.150
and so, like the first time you have a shadow

00:02:41.150 --> 00:02:43.120
cast by the moon, you're like, what?

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:44.620
What's casting that shadow?

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:46.360
- I was like, does this mean I'm a werewolf?

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:48.424
I thought moonlight was like,

00:02:48.424 --> 00:02:50.300
I don't know, like passenger pigeons,

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:53.320
like something that had a time that had passed.

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:55.180
(Hank laughs)

00:02:55.180 --> 00:02:57.130
- It was just over somehow?
- Yeah.

00:02:57.130 --> 00:02:58.640
Hank, do you remember your first tweet?

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:01.060
Don't worry, I already wrote it down
in case you don't remember.

00:03:01.060 --> 00:03:03.520
- It was probably like, I'm starting up Twitter now,

00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:04.570
let's see how that goes.

00:03:04.570 --> 00:03:06.080
- No, that was my first tweet.
(both laugh)

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:08.270
Your first tweet was in June of 2007

00:03:08.270 --> 00:03:10.250
back on your Ecogeek handle--
- Oh!

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:12.770
- and it was, "Writing up some stories for Ecogeek.

00:03:12.770 --> 00:03:15.524
Wondering when Google will buy Twitter."

00:03:15.524 --> 00:03:17.510
- Oh, if only they had.

00:03:17.510 --> 00:03:20.480
- Yeah, I mean it still kind of makes sense.

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:21.940
- But Google has such a successful

00:03:21.940 --> 00:03:24.020
existing social network in Google+.

00:03:24.020 --> 00:03:28.680
Hank, when was the last time
you did something for the first time?

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:31.610
- It's the first time I've had all of these cells.

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:36.200
It's the first time that
I've probably ever worn this outfit.

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:38.865
- Do you know the last time
you'll do something for the first time?

00:03:38.865 --> 00:03:40.780
- Ai yi yi.
- (whispers) Death.

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:42.740
Okay, Hank, DFTBA. I will see you...

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:43.610
- Right now.

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:45.140
- I'll continue to see you.
- Yeah.

